# ai-slop-gate — Trivy vulnerability ignore list
# Only CVEs confirmed unreachable in our usage, or waiting on an
# upstream release we don't control. Review dates are attached via
# `exp:YYYY-MM-DD` — Trivy stops ignoring automatically after that
# date, so re-run `trivy image` then and remove the line if a fix
# has landed, or extend the date if still waiting.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# perl-base (Debian essential package, pulled in by dpkg/apt itself —
# cannot be removed. We never invoke perl or any perl module.)
# No fixed version from Debian security team yet for most of these.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
CVE-2026-13221
CVE-2026-42496
CVE-2026-8376
CVE-2026-42497
CVE-2026-48962
CVE-2026-57432
CVE-2026-57433
CVE-2026-9538

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# usr/local/bin/trivy and usr/local/bin/syft (vendored Go binaries
# from aquasec/trivy and ghcr.io/anchore/syft — we don't control
# their build; waiting on next upstream release with patched deps)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
CVE-2026-84304 exp:2026-09-20
CVE-2026-27145 exp:2026-09-20
CVE-2026-33818 exp:2026-09-20
CVE-2026-39821 exp:2026-09-20
CVE-2026-39822 exp:2026-09-20
CVE-2026-42504 exp:2026-09-20
CVE-2026-46600 exp:2026-09-20
CVE-2026-56853 exp:2026-09-20
CVE-2026-56858 exp:2026-09-20
CVE-2026-56859 exp:2026-09-20
CVE-2026-56860 exp:2026-09-20
CVE-2026-56862 exp:2026-09-20

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# npm's own internal vendored copies (usr/local/lib/node_modules/npm/
# node_modules/*) — build-time tool only, not our application code.
# Our own dependencies (tar, brace-expansion, ip-address in
# package.json) are already patched to safe versions.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
